abstract: >
  This software applies ChronoGauge, a bagging ensemble of 100 neural network
  circadian time predictors, to all processed Arabidopsis thaliana spaceflight
  transcriptomics data from NASA GeneLab (23 studies, 603 samples). It quantifies
  circadian phase shifts between spaceflight and ground control samples using
  Watson-Williams tests and random-effects meta-analysis (metafor). The analysis
  is performed in two forks: Fork A (14 accessions from Barker 2023) and Fork B
  (all Arabidopsis spaceflight transcriptomics). Results show a small but
  significant overall phase advance under spaceflight (-0.09 h, p = 0.046),
  with the strongest effect in root tissue (-0.17 h, p < 0.001).
